message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Engineering ATLAS: the dynamic-range law and its retraction ledger"
abstract: >-
  An instrument short of dynamic range does not return a cautious answer. It
  reports that the quantity is bounded, which is the most reassuring wrong
  answer available. This work derives the critical headroom below which a
  maximum-likelihood generalised-Pareto fit crosses into that failure, as the
  root of E[Z^2] = 2 (E[Z])^2 on the censored observable; establishes that the
  failure belongs to the estimator rather than the instrument, since Hill is
  structurally blind to it and Pickands avoids rather than corrects it; and
  publishes a ledger of every claim the project itself withdrew.
type: software
